\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Does every closed hyperbolicity cone $K(p,e)$ of a real homogeneous polynomial hyperbolic in direction $e$ admit a finite exact semidefinite lift? This means
\[
K(p,e)=\left\{x:\text{there exists }u\in\mathbb{R}^a\text{ with }A_0+\sum_i x_iA_i+\sum_j u_jB_j\succeq0\right\}
\]
for some finite $a$ and finite real symmetric matrices, where $\succeq0$ means positive semidefinite; no closure of the projection is allowed.

\subsection{Short English statement}
For every real homogeneous polynomial hyperbolic in direction $e$, is its closed cone $K(p,e)$ exactly the set of $x$ for which some $u\in\mathbb{R}^a$ makes $A_0+\sum_i x_iA_i+\sum_j u_jB_j$ positive semidefinite, for some finite $a$ and finite real symmetric matrices, without taking the closure of the projection?

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] Original question source or mathematical context.
\url{https://aimath.org/WWN/matrixineq/matrixineq.pdf}.
\item[S2] Original question source or mathematical context.
\url{https://doi.org/10.1016/j.indag.2025.06.008}.
\item[S3] Original question source or mathematical context.
\url{https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2014/17}.
\item[S4] OpenAI, manuscript citation page. Source of the formulation motivating this local problem.
\url{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/Hyperbolicity-Cones-Without-Semidefinite-Lifts-October-5-2026/README.md}.
\end{itemize}

